// CROWN — latency rides an effect op's fn-typed PARAMETER: a performing
// closure handed to `run`, called by the handler's arm, the install under
// `with !E`. Expect E_EffectMismatch.
//
// Checked clean and ran at 7 through the pinned boot (measured 2026-09-23):
// the param's row cell rides the effect as a TYPE argument (`Run(r)`), and
// unify no-ops on a row-sorted node, so the arm's call charges a cell the
// perform never reaches.
effect E { op() -> Int }
effect Run { run(f: () -> Int) -> Int }
fn loud() = op()
handler runner { run(f) => resume(f()) }
fn body() = run(loud)
fn bad() with !E = body() ~> runner
handler h { op() => resume(7) }
fn main() = bad() ~> h
